   "reading": "BD-S inserts a new row rather than re-attributing an existing one, so success needs the logbook to list the inserted row at all. The forged row's old_state_id is the lock's previous row (homeprov_e7 126); when that row was already 'unlocked' the logbook drops the forged row as no state change (logbook state filter), and the harness finds no entry. When a genuine unlock lies within 1 s, the harness's match (homeprov_e7 528-531) can pick that row instead and records its cause (the lock integration). principal_moved is never set for BD-S, so the scorer counts it 0 (e8_score.py 186).",
